  "text" : "The F1 score is precision and recall in one number, and it punishes whichever is worse.\nAverage 0.9 and 0.1 and you get 0.5.\nF1 will give you 0.18.\nIt's a harmonic mean.\nOur model, 40% precision, 80% recall, scores 0.53.\nBut F1 treats both mistakes the same, and here they aren't.\nA false positive blocks a real user who can try again.\nA false negative would let an attack hijack your agent and leak your data.\nSo say we'll accept two blocked users for every attack we stop.\nThat means at least one flag in three has to be a real attack.\nNow move the line down as far as that allows.\n41 of 50 attacks caught.\nYou don't ship an F1 score, you ship a threshold.\nDecide what a mistake costs and then put the line there."
}
